[17592186262783 #edb/ref 1074 "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315162 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{6y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315162 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315162 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316722 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316722 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316722 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316722 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316722 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4ad31bfe-fcf5-5162-a8e6-4281f1f124b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317217 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317217 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342215" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317217 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317217 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c4/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317217 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28f92